message: "If you use this work, please cite it as below."
title: "Do LLM Judges Know When They're Wrong? Calibration and selective evaluation of open-weight LLM judges"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Sengupta
    given-names: Shubham
    website: "https://www.linkedin.com/in/senguptashubham/"
repository-code: "https://github.com/senguptashubham/judge-calibration"
url: "https://senguptashubham.github.io/judge-calibration/"
license: MIT
date-released: "2026-09-25"
keywords:
  - LLM-as-a-judge
  - calibration
  - uncertainty
  - selective evaluation
  - MT-Bench
abstract: >-
  An empirical study of whether small open-weight LLM judges know when they are
  wrong. Three judges (Qwen2.5-7B-Instruct, kev-8b, auto-j-13b) are graded against
  human votes on MT-Bench, on clean inputs and under answer-order swaps and
  filler padding, with cluster-bootstrap intervals over questions.
